<p>President Donald Trump hosted the first meeting of his newly created “Board of Peace” in Washington, bringing together representatives from 27 countries, with another 21 countries and the European Union attending as observers, to discuss next steps in a Trump-brokered Gaza peace and reconstruction effort. Trump said nine countries pledged nearly $7 billion for a Gaza relief and rebuilding package, and five countries agreed to provide thousands of troops for an international stabilization force in the territory. The administration and several participating governments framed the announcements as a shift from broad plans to on-the-ground work. Even so, some outlets underscored big unanswered questions about how the plan would work in practice—especially disarmament, governance, and representation—after reports that only one Palestinian attended the gathering. Despite the uncertainties, the meeting produced tangible commitments that—if delivered—could provide an early pool of resources and coordination for rebuilding.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/gt6tGJskfZNCU7hEvdUrFP7kIse54m18Rt0U2NWw01LuEiQe4Ep9MwuUkfhhPr0_dez_9mC8VIvGrDJpsdG4BFvxzHbZEYwFeKc7b9tVzhey8qaSoBDr2YP1SJcidPN4' alt='President Donald Trump gavels out inaugural Board of Peace meeting' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>US funding pledge: Trump also said the United States would contribute $10 billion to the board, but he did not say how the money would be used or whether Congress had agreed to fund it.</li><li>Central Asia outreach: Coverage portrayed Kazakhstan and Uzbekistan’s Gaza reconstruction pledges as a bid to deepen ties with Washington and seek stronger US geopolitical backing.</li><li>Political tone: Some coverage said the event’s staging kept the focus squarely on Trump, while still treating the financial commitments as concrete.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Donald Trump: Trump pitched the Board of Peace as a high-status forum, calling it the “most prestigious board ever put together”. (<a href='https://theweek.com/politics/trump-board-of-peace-meeting'>The Week</a>)</li><li>Al Jazeera (Inside Story): The outlet highlighted the limited Palestinian presence at the meeting and centered its discussion on what that could mean for Gaza’s political and humanitarian future. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/inside-story/2026/2/20/whats-next-for-gaza-after-trumps-board-of-peace-meets-in-washington'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Euronews: Euronews framed the Washington meeting as a step toward implementation, including reconstruction, infrastructure rebuilding, and possible troop deployments under a US-backed stabilization framework for the Strip. (<a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/02/20/troop-and-funding-pledges-come-in-for-trumps-gaza-plan'>Euronews</a>)</li><li>AllSides fact check team (via NBC): The fact-check write-up focused less on the pledges themselves and more on the unresolved mechanics—how the initiative would work in practice and how financing might be divided. (<a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-02-20-0800/foreign-policy-fact-check-team-rebuilding-gaza-how-will-it-work-who-foots-bill'>AllSides</a>)</li><li>RFE/RL: RFE/RL portrayed Kazakhstan and Uzbekistan’s pledges as part of a broader push to build closer relations with the United States and strengthen their geopolitical positioning. (<a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/kazakhstan-uzbekistan-gaza-reconstruction-us-ties/33683513.html'>RFE/RL</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://theweek.com/politics/trump-board-of-peace-meeting'>Trump touts pledges at 1st Board of Peace meeting</a> - theweek.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/inside-story/2026/2/20/whats-next-for-gaza-after-trumps-board-of-peace-meets-in-washington'>What’s next for Gaza after Trump’s Board of Peace meets in Washington?</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/kazakhstan-uzbekistan-gaza-reconstruction-us-ties/33683513.html'>Kazakh, Uzbek Leaders Seek Trump Approval With Gaza Peace Pledges</a> - rferl.org</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/02/20/troop-and-funding-pledges-come-in-for-trumps-gaza-plan'>Troop and funding pledges come in for Trump&#x27;s Gaza plan</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-02-20-0800/foreign-policy-fact-check-team-rebuilding-gaza-how-will-it-work-who-foots-bill'>Fact Check Team: Rebuilding Gaza, how will it work &amp; who foots the bill?</a> - allsides.com</li></ul>